.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt CLOSE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm close
.Nd close a scheme-file handle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x64).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call is part of the scheme IPC protocol (see
.Xr scheme 7
and
.Pa architecture/03-system-servers.md ).
.Pp
For a filesystem handle,
.Nm
releases one reference to the open-file description.  The server removes the
description and its cursor only when the last reference is closed.  A
.Xr dup 2
duplicate or a transferred reference keeps the description alive.
.Pp
The kernel closes the local handle immediately but sends the protocol CLOSE only
when the last kernel reference (including attachments, transfers and in-flight
requests) is gone.  It sends one CLOSE per server reference, so the server's
reference count reaches zero at the same time.  A dying process closes every
handle it owned exactly once; one-way CLOSE notifications are delivered even
after the client is gone.
.Pp
When the last reference to an unlinked file is closed, the server releases the
inode and its data.  A process that dies closes every handle it owned exactly
once; a transferred reference in another process still keeps the description
alive.
.Pp
Closing an unknown or already closed server file id returns
.Er EBADF .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er -offset indent
.It Er EBADF
The handle is not a scheme-file handle or is already closed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dup 2 ,
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
